1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,585
WOMAN:

2
00:00:00,585 --> 00:00:04,320
I’ve been meaning to ask you for some advice about restaurants.

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:04,822
WOMAN:

4
00:00:04,822 --> 00:00:09,157
I need to book somewhere to celebrate my sister’s 30th birthday

5
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:12,710
and I liked the sound of that place you went to for your mum’s

6
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:13,010
50th.

7
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:13,090
MAN:

8
00:00:13,090 --> 00:00:13,632
The Junction?

9
00:00:13,632 --> 00:00:17,617
Yeah, I’d definitely recommend that for a special occasion.

10
00:00:17,617 --> 00:00:19,743
We had a great time there.

11
00:00:19,743 --> 00:00:21,160
Everyone really enjoyed it.

12
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:21,506
WOMAN:

13
00:00:21,506 --> 00:00:22,888
Where is it again?

14
00:00:22,888 --> 00:00:24,270
I can’t remember.

15
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:24,589
MAN:

16
00:00:24,589 --> 00:00:29,050
It’s on Greyson Street, only about a two minute walk from the station.

17
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:29,340
WOMAN:

18
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:29,630
Oh,

19
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:30,500
that’s good.

20
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,110
I’d prefer not to have to drive anywhere.

21
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:36,590
But I don’t want to have to walk too far either.

22
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:36,959
MAN:

23
00:00:36,959 --> 00:00:42,121
Yes, the location’s perfect but that’s not necessarily why I’d recommend

24
00:00:42,121 --> 00:00:42,490
it.

25
00:00:42,490 --> 00:00:42,915
MAN:

26
00:00:42,915 --> 00:00:44,616
The food’s amazing.

27
00:00:44,616 --> 00:00:50,570
If you like fish it’s probably the best restaurant in town for that.

28
00:00:50,570 --> 00:00:50,917
MAN:

29
00:00:50,917 --> 00:00:55,781
It’s always really fresh and there are lots of interesting dishes to choose

30
00:00:55,781 --> 00:00:56,128
from.

31
00:00:56,128 --> 00:00:58,560
But all the food is good there.

32
00:00:58,560 --> 00:00:59,060
WOMAN:

33
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,060
Is it really expensive?

34
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:01,409
MAN:

35
00:01:01,409 --> 00:01:06,291
It’s certainly not cheap but for a special occasion I think it’s

36
00:01:06,291 --> 00:01:06,640
fine.

37
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:06,979
MAN:

38
00:01:06,979 --> 00:01:12,396
It’s got a great atmosphere and before dinner you can go up on the roof

39
00:01:12,396 --> 00:01:13,750
and have a drink.

40
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:14,109
MAN:

41
00:01:14,109 --> 00:01:18,053
It’s really nice up there but you need to book.

42
00:01:18,053 --> 00:01:21,280
It’s very popular as the views are spectacular.

43
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:21,707
WOMAN:

44
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:22,560
Sounds good.

45
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:25,547
So that’s definitely a possibility then.

46
00:01:25,547 --> 00:01:28,960
Is there anywhere else you can think of?

47
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:29,376
MAN:

48
00:01:29,376 --> 00:01:34,790
If you want somewhere a bit less formal then you could try Paloma.

49
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:35,004
WOMAN:

50
00:01:35,004 --> 00:01:35,646
Where’s that?

51
00:01:35,646 --> 00:01:36,930
I haven’t heard of it.

52
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:37,257
MAN:

53
00:01:37,257 --> 00:01:38,894
No, it’s quite new.

54
00:01:38,894 --> 00:01:43,803
It’s only been open a few months but it’s got a great reputation

55
00:01:43,803 --> 00:01:44,130
already.

56
00:01:44,130 --> 00:01:47,730
It’s in a really beautiful old building on Bow Street.

57
00:01:47,730 --> 00:01:48,117
WOMAN:

58
00:01:48,117 --> 00:01:52,760
Oh, I think I know where you mean – right beside the cinema?

59
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:53,092
MAN:

60
00:01:53,092 --> 00:01:53,423
Yes,

61
00:01:53,423 --> 00:01:54,418
that’s it.

62
00:01:54,418 --> 00:01:59,060
I’ve only been there a couple of times but I was really impressed.

63
00:01:59,060 --> 00:01:59,406
MAN:

64
00:01:59,406 --> 00:02:02,869
The chef used to work at Don Felipe’s, apparently.

65
00:02:02,869 --> 00:02:05,640
I was really sorry when that closed down.

66
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:05,953
WOMAN:

67
00:02:05,953 --> 00:02:08,770
So is all the food they serve Spanish, then?

68
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:09,077
MAN:

69
00:02:09,077 --> 00:02:09,385
Yeah.

70
00:02:09,385 --> 00:02:13,379
You can get lots of small dishes to share – which always works really

71
00:02:13,379 --> 00:02:15,530
well if you’re in a group.

72
00:02:15,530 --> 00:02:15,962
WOMAN:

73
00:02:15,962 --> 00:02:16,394
Mmm.

74
00:02:16,394 --> 00:02:17,690
Worth thinking about.

75
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:18,059
MAN:

76
00:02:18,059 --> 00:02:18,429
Yeah.

77
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:22,491
There’s a lively atmosphere and the waiters are really friendly.

78
00:02:22,491 --> 00:02:27,661
The only thing is that you need to pay a £50 deposit to book

79
00:02:27,661 --> 00:02:28,400
a table.

80
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:28,699
WOMAN:

81
00:02:28,699 --> 00:02:31,390
A lot of restaurants are doing that these days.

82
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:31,686
WOMAN:

83
00:02:31,686 --> 00:02:36,133
I should have a look at the menu to check there’s a good choice

84
00:02:36,133 --> 00:02:37,022
of vegetarian dishes.

85
00:02:37,022 --> 00:02:39,690
A couple of my friends have stopped eating meat.

86
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:40,044
MAN:

87
00:02:40,044 --> 00:02:40,753
Not sure.

88
00:02:40,753 --> 00:02:44,650
I’d say the selection of those would be quite limited.

89
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:44,951
MAN:

90
00:02:44,951 --> 00:02:47,061
I’ve just thought of another idea.

91
00:02:47,061 --> 00:02:48,870
Have you been to The Audley?

92
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:49,196
WOMAN:

93
00:02:49,196 --> 00:02:52,134
No, don’t think I’ve heard of it.

94
00:02:52,134 --> 00:02:53,440
How’s it spelt?

95
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:53,939
MAN:

96
00:02:53,939 --> 00:02:54,439
A-U-D-L-E-Y.

97
00:02:54,439 --> 00:03:01,431
You must have heard of it – there’s been a lot about it in

98
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:02,430
the press.

99
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:02,757
WOMAN:

100
00:03:02,757 --> 00:03:07,006
I don’t tend to pay much attention to that kind of thing.

101
00:03:07,006 --> 00:03:08,640
So where is it exactly?

102
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:08,997
MAN:

103
00:03:08,997 --> 00:03:13,280
It’s in that hotel near Baxter Bridge – on the top floor.

104
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:13,623
WOMAN:

105
00:03:13,623 --> 00:03:16,710
Oh, the views would be incredible from up there.

106
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:17,034
MAN:

107
00:03:17,034 --> 00:03:17,358
Yeah.

108
00:03:17,358 --> 00:03:18,979
I’d love to go.

109
00:03:18,979 --> 00:03:24,166
I can’t think of the chef’s name but she was a judge on that

110
00:03:24,166 --> 00:03:25,462
TV cookery show recently.

111
00:03:25,462 --> 00:03:28,380
And she’s written a couple of cookery books.

112
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:28,978
WOMAN:

113
00:03:28,978 --> 00:03:30,770
Oh, Angela Frayn.

114
00:03:30,770 --> 00:03:31,186
MAN:

115
00:03:31,186 --> 00:03:32,850
That’s the one.

116
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:37,010
Anyway, it’s had excellent reviews from all the newspapers.

117
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:37,368
WOMAN:

118
00:03:37,368 --> 00:03:40,590
That would be a memorable place for a celebration.

119
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:40,975
MAN:

120
00:03:40,975 --> 00:03:41,360
Definitely.

121
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:47,139
Obviously it’s worth going there just for the view but the food is supposed

122
00:03:47,139 --> 00:03:48,680
to be really special.

123
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:49,052
WOMAN:

124
00:03:49,052 --> 00:03:52,770
She only likes cooking with local products, doesn’t she?

125
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:53,208
MAN:

126
00:03:53,208 --> 00:03:53,645
Yes.

127
00:03:53,645 --> 00:03:58,897
Everything at the restaurant has to be sourced within a short distance

128
00:03:58,897 --> 00:04:01,960
and absolutely nothing flown in from abroad.

129
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:02,346
WOMAN:

130
00:04:02,346 --> 00:04:05,050
I imagine it’s really expensive though.

131
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:05,455
MAN:

132
00:04:05,455 --> 00:04:08,692
Well, you could go for the set lunch.

133
00:04:08,692 --> 00:04:12,334
That’s quite reasonable for a top class restaurant:

134
00:04:12,334 --> 00:04:13,548
£30 a head.

135
00:04:13,548 --> 00:04:18,000
In the evening I think it’d be more like £50.

136
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:18,347
WOMAN:

137
00:04:18,347 --> 00:04:20,426
At least that, I should think.

138
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:23,198
But I’m sure everyone would enjoy it.

139
00:04:23,198 --> 00:04:28,050
It’s not the kind of place you leave feeling hungry though, is it?

140
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:29,090
With tiny portions?

141
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:29,448
MAN:

142
00:04:29,448 --> 00:04:33,024
No, the reviews I’ve read didn’t mention that.

143
00:04:33,024 --> 00:04:35,170
I imagine they’d be average.

144
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:35,719
WOMAN:

145
00:04:35,719 --> 00:04:36,267
Well,

146
00:04:36,267 --> 00:04:39,010
that’s all great, thanks …
